IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sca-nouns`
IMPORT `sca-p1-preliminary`
IMPORT `sca-p4-civil-district`

-- State Courts Act 1970 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition -- LAYER 1, PART 4 (second part): CRIMINAL JURISDICTION OF DISTRICT COURTS (ss 50), JURISDICTION OF MAGISTRATES' COURTS (ss 51, 52, 54, 54AA).
-- The Magistrate's Court limit is a parameter of each function that needs it; the caller takes it from `s 2 "Magistrate's Court limit" the amount in dollars` (the Act's $60,000 unless an order under s 52(3) specifies another amount).
-- Section 52(3), like s 30, is a power to vary a limit by order; it is machinery (inert, reason 2), and its effect is carried by the limit parameters.

§ `Sections 50 and 51 -- criminal jurisdiction`

-- src:1510 | 50.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), a District Court exercising
-- src:1511 | criminal jurisdiction has —
-- src:1513 | (a) the jurisdiction and powers conferred on it by the Criminal
-- src:1514 | Procedure Code 2010 and any other written law; and
@ref s 50(1)(a) (src:1510-1514)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `it is exercising criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the jurisdiction or power is conferred on it by the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or any other written law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1)(a) a District Court exercising criminal jurisdiction has the jurisdiction or power` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `District Court` AND `it is exercising criminal jurisdiction` AND `the jurisdiction or power is conferred on it by the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 or any other written law`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (2)" and the grant is of what "the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 and any other written law" confer, which are not among the sources
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1516 | (b) without limiting paragraph (a), the power to order medical
-- src:1517 | examination of a person who is an accused in any criminal
-- src:1518 | proceedings where the physical or mental condition of the
-- src:1519 | person is relevant to any matter in question in the
-- src:1520 | proceedings.
@ref s 50(1)(b) (src:1516-1520)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `it is exercising criminal jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the physical or mental condition of the accused is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(1)(b) a District Court has the power to order the medical examination of the accused` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "a District Court exercising criminal jurisdiction"
        IF NOT (court EQUALS `District Court` AND `it is exercising criminal jurisdiction`) THEN NOTHING
        IF `the physical or mental condition of the accused is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the power to order medical examination of a person who is an accused in any criminal proceedings where the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1524 | (2) The criminal jurisdiction of a District Court is exercisable
-- src:1525 | where the offence is committed —
-- src:1527 | (a) within Singapore;
-- src:1529 | (b) on board any ship or aircraft registered in Singapore;
-- src:1531 | (c) by any person who is a citizen of Singapore on the high
-- src:1532 | seas or on any aircraft; and
-- src:1534 | (d) in any place or by any person if it is provided in any written
-- src:1535 | law that the offence is triable in Singapore.
@ref s 50(2)(a) to (d) (src:1524-1535)
GIVEN `the offence is committed within Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed on board a ship or aircraft registered in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offence is committed by a citizen of Singapore on the high seas or on an aircraft` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law provides that the offence is triable in Singapore, in the place or by the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 50(2) the criminal jurisdiction of a District Court is exercisable over the offence` MEANS
    IF `the offence is committed within Singapore` OR `the offence is committed on board a ship or aircraft registered in Singapore` OR `the offence is committed by a citizen of Singapore on the high seas or on an aircraft` OR `a written law provides that the offence is triable in Singapore, in the place or by the person`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is exercisable where the offence is committed — (a) ...; (b) ...; (c) ...; and (d) ..." (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
         JUST FALSE

