§ `Section 52 -- civil jurisdiction of Magistrates' Courts`

-- src:1573 | 52.—(1) Subject to subsection (1A), a Magistrate’s Court has all
-- src:1574 | the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and
-- src:1575 | try any action in personam where —
-- src:1577 | (a) the defendant is served with an originating claim or any
-- src:1578 | other originating process —
-- src:1580 | (i) in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of
-- src:1581 | Court; or
-- src:1583 | (ii) outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by
-- src:1584 | and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court; or
-- src:1588 | (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of a Magistrate’s
-- src:1589 | Court.
@ref s 52(1)(a) and (b) (src:1573-1589)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1) a Magistrate's Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of jurisdiction "to hear and try any action in personam"
        IF NOT (proceeding's `the action is in personam`) THEN NOTHING
        IF proceeding's `the defendant was served in Singapore in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court`
           OR proceeding's `the defendant was served outside Singapore in the circumstances authorised by and in the manner prescribed by Rules of Court`
           OR proceeding's `the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of the court asked about`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where — (a) the defendant is served ... (i) in Singapore ... or (ii) outside Singapore ...; or (b) the defendant submits to the jurisdiction of a Magistrate's Court" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- src:1593 | (1A) The jurisdiction of a Magistrate’s Court under subsection (1)
-- src:1594 | does not include jurisdiction to hear and try any action where —
-- src:1596 | (a) there is no claim for any sum of money;
-- src:1598 | (aa) the action is in passing off;
-- src:1602 | (b) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the Magistrate’s
-- src:1603 | Court limit; or
-- src:1605 | (c) any remedy or relief sought in the action, in addition or as
-- src:1606 | an alternative to the amount claimed in the action, is in
-- src:1611 | respect of a subject matter the value of which exceeds the
-- src:1612 | Magistrate’s Court limit.
@ref s 52(1A)(a), (aa), (b) and (c) (src:1593-1612)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1A) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the Magistrate's Court limit` MEANS
    proceeding's `the amount claimed in dollars` GREATER THAN `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars`
    OR proceeding's `the value in dollars of the subject matter of any remedy or relief sought` GREATER THAN `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars`

@ref s 52(1A) (src:1593-1612)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 52(1A) the action falls within a class that subsection (1A) excludes from a Magistrate's Court's jurisdiction` MEANS
    (NOT (proceeding's `the claim includes a claim for a sum of money`))
    OR (proceeding's `the action is in passing off`)
    OR (`s 52(1A) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the Magistrate's Court limit` proceeding `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars`)

@ref s 52(1A) (src:1593-1612)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1A) a Magistrate's Court's jurisdiction under subsection (1) includes the action` MEANS
    IF `s 52(1A) the action falls within a class that subsection (1A) excludes from a Magistrate's Court's jurisdiction` proceeding `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars`
    THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The jurisdiction of a Magistrate’s Court under subsection (1) does not include jurisdiction to hear and try any action where — (a) there is no claim for any sum of money; (aa) the action is in passing off; (b) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the Magistrate’s Court limit; or (c) any remedy or relief sought ... exceeds the Magistrate’s Court limit"
         JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an action outside those classes is not mentioned in subsection (1A), which grants nothing
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1616 | (1B) A Magistrate’s Court has, in any proceedings within its
-- src:1617 | jurisdiction under subsection (1) —
-- src:1619 | (a) the power —
-- src:1621 | (i) to grant such relief, redress or remedy or
-- src:1622 | combination of remedies, either absolute or
-- src:1623 | conditional; and
-- src:1625 | (ii) to give such and the like effect to every ground of
-- src:1626 | defence or counterclaim equitable or legal,
-- src:1628 | (a) as ought to be granted or given in the like action by the
-- src:1629 | General Division of the High Court and in as full and
-- src:1630 | ample a manner;
-- src:1632 | (b) without limiting paragraph (a), the power —
-- src:1634 | (i) to grant an injunction;
-- src:1636 | (ii) to make binding declarations of rights; and
-- src:1638 | (iii) to order medical examination of a person who is a
-- src:1639 | party to any proceedings where the physical or
-- src:1640 | mental condition of the person is relevant to any
-- src:1641 | matter in question in the proceedings;
-- src:1643 | (c) the power to make any order or to exercise any authority or
-- src:1644 | jurisdiction which, if it related to a proceeding pending in
-- src:1645 | the General Division of the High Court, might be made or
-- src:1646 | exercised by a Judge sitting in chambers in the General
-- src:1647 | Division of the High Court; and
-- src:1649 | (d) the powers conferred on a District Court by —
-- src:1651 | (i) sections 43 and 49A; and
-- src:1655 | (ii) section 12 of the Civil Law Act 1909.
@ref s 52(1B)(a) to (d) (src:1616-1655)
GIVEN `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A `Power of a court in a civil action`
      `the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1B) the Magistrate's Court has the power in the proceedings` MEANS
    CONSIDER power
    WHEN `Grant any relief, redress or remedy, or combination of remedies, absolute or conditional` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Give effect to every ground of defence or counterclaim, equitable or legal` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Grant an injunction` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Make a binding declaration of rights` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Order the medical examination of a party` THEN
        IF NOT (`the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question in the proceedings`)
        THEN -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the power ... to order medical examination of a person who is a party to any proceedings where the physical or mental condition of the person is relevant to any matter in question" (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))
             JUST FALSE
        ELSE `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Make an order or exercise an authority which a Judge in chambers in the General Division of the High Court could make or exercise` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Exercise a power that section 43 or 49A gives a District Court` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    WHEN `Exercise a power that section 12 of the Civil Law Act 1909 gives a District Court` THEN `s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): paragraph (b) says "without limiting paragraph (a)"; the section does not say a Magistrate's Court has no other power
    WHEN `Another power` THEN NOTHING

@ref s 52(1B) (src:1616-1655)
GIVEN `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(1B) the power is conferred if the proceedings are within the jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF `the action is within the jurisdiction of the Magistrate's Court under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the powers are given "in any proceedings within its jurisdiction under subsection (1)"; the subsection says nothing of proceedings outside it
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1659 | (2) In exercising its jurisdiction under subsection (1) or powers
-- src:1660 | under subsection (1B), a Magistrate’s Court is subject to the same
-- src:1665 | limitations and provisions as are applicable to a District Court under
-- src:1666 | this Act.
@ref s 52(2) (src:1659-1666)
GIVEN `the limitation or provision is applicable to a District Court under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52(2) a Magistrate's Court is subject to the limitation or provision in exercising its jurisdiction or powers` MEANS
    IF `the limitation or provision is applicable to a District Court under this Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection borrows "the same limitations and provisions as are applicable to a District Court"; it says nothing of a limitation or provision that does not apply to a District Court (section 52(1A), for example, is the Magistrate's Court's own)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 52, read with s 19(3) and s 52(2) (gathered by hand) (src:1573-1666)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `Civil action`
      `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 52 a Magistrate's Court has jurisdiction over the action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): s 52(1) is for "any action in personam"
        IF `s 52(1) a Magistrate's Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` proceeding EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): s 52(2) borrows the limitations of a District Court, including s 19(3) "Subject to section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 and any order under subsection (1) thereof"
        IF `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE AND proceeding's `section 28A of the Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969, or an order under its subsection (1), affects the action` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 52(2) "a Magistrate’s Court is subject to the same limitations and provisions as are applicable to a District Court under this Act" and s 19(3) "does not include"
        IF `s 19(3) the action falls within a class that subsection (3) excludes from a District Court's jurisdiction` proceeding EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 52(1) "where" is not met
        IF `s 52(1) a Magistrate's Court has the jurisdiction of the General Division of the High Court to hear and try the action` proceeding EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 52(1A)(a) and (aa) "does not include ... any action where — (a) there is no claim for any sum of money; (aa) the action is in passing off"
        IF (NOT (proceeding's `the claim includes a claim for a sum of money`)) OR (proceeding's `the action is in passing off`) THEN JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (`s 52(1A) the amount claimed or the value of the subject matter of the remedy or relief exceeds the Magistrate's Court limit` proceeding `the Magistrate's Court limit in dollars`) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): over the limit, but the claimant has abandoned the excess or the parties have agreed; sections 22 and 23 name "a District Court" and section 52(2) borrows a District Court's "limitations and provisions" without saying that these two are among them (fork F-S52(2))
        IF proceeding's `the claimant has abandoned the excess amount or the remedy or relief` OR proceeding's `the parties agreed, by a memorandum signed by them or their solicitors, that the court is to have jurisdiction` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 52(1A)(b) and (c) "does not include ... any action where — (b) the amount claimed in the action exceeds the Magistrate’s Court limit; or (c) any remedy or relief sought ... exceeds the Magistrate’s Court limit"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Sections 54 and 54AA -- judgments of Magistrates' Courts; agreement not to appeal`

-- src:1677 | 54. Every judgment or order of a Magistrate’s Court in the exercise
-- src:1678 | of its civil jurisdiction has the same effect (for purposes of appeal or
-- src:1679 | otherwise) and is to be enforced in the same manner as if it were given
-- src:1680 | or made by a District Court.
@ref s 54 (src:1677-1680)
GIVEN court IS A `Court or tribunal`
      `it is a judgment or order in the exercise of its civil jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54 the judgment or order has the same effect and is enforced in the same manner as if given by a District Court` MEANS
    IF court EQUALS `Magistrate's Court` AND `it is a judgment or order in the exercise of its civil jurisdiction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about "Every judgment or order of a Magistrate’s Court in the exercise of its civil jurisdiction"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1684 | 54AA.—(1) An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a
-- src:1685 | Magistrate’s Court exercising civil jurisdiction, where the parties
-- src:1686 | have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the
-- src:1687 | decision is final, unless the party seeking to appeal proves that —
-- src:1689 | (a) the decision is affected by fraud or illegality; or
-- src:1691 | (b) there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural
-- src:1692 | justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision.
@ref s 54AA(1)(a) and (b) (src:1684-1692)
GIVEN `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54AA(1) an appeal can be brought against the decision of a Magistrate's Court exercising civil jurisdiction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on an appeal "where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final"; without that agreement the subsection says nothing of whether an appeal can be brought (the right of appeal is outside the sources)
        IF NOT (`the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final`) THEN NOTHING
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the party seeking to appeal proves that — (a) ...; or (b) ..."; where the party proves fraud, illegality or a fundamental breach of natural justice the bar is lifted and a lifted bar grants nothing (QA)
        IF `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` OR `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` THEN NOTHING
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An appeal cannot be brought against a decision of a Magistrate’s Court exercising civil jurisdiction, where the parties have agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final, unless ..."
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

@ref s 54AA(1) (src:1684-1692)
GIVEN `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54AA(1) the bar on an appeal applies to the decision` MEANS
    IF `the parties agreed in writing signed by or on behalf of each party that the decision is final`
       AND NOT (`the party seeking to appeal proves that the decision is affected by fraud or illegality` OR `the party seeking to appeal proves that there was a fundamental breach of the rules of natural justice in the proceedings resulting in the decision`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the bar is "where the parties have agreed in writing ... that the decision is final, unless" the appellant proves fraud, illegality or a fundamental breach (a "where" that is not met answers JUST FALSE; "unless" lifts the bar)
         JUST FALSE

-- src:1694 | (2) An agreement mentioned in subsection (1) —
-- src:1696 | (a) may be made before or after the decision to which the
-- src:1697 | agreement relates is made; and
@ref s 54AA(2)(a) (src:1694-1697)
GIVEN when IS A `When an agreement was made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54AA(2) an agreement mentioned in subsection (1) may be made at that time` MEANS
    CONSIDER when
    WHEN `Before the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `After the decision was made` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection says the agreement "may be made before or after the decision" and says nothing of any other time
    WHEN `At another time` THEN NOTHING

-- src:1699 | (b) may relate to part of a decision, in which case references in
-- src:1700 | subsection (1) to a decision are to be read as references to
-- src:1701 | that part of the decision.
@ref s 54AA(2)(b) (src:1699-1701)
GIVEN `the agreement relates to part of a decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 54AA(2) the references in subsection (1) to a decision are references to that part of the decision` MEANS
    IF `the agreement relates to part of a decision`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in which case" - the reading as that part applies where the agreement relates to part of a decision; for an agreement about the whole decision the paragraph is silent
    ELSE NOTHING
